export abstract anchor FactoryVerification:
    conformanceReport:
        A report records checklist version, specVersion, implementationVersion,
        actor and independence, scenario identifier, capability mapping,
        invocation, observed value, evidence reference and hash, timestamps, and
        a verdict. The report is an artifact under the evidence rules. The
        checklist and report are versioned with the specification.
    conformanceIndependence:
        The verifier is a different agent or session from the implementation
        work, did not author the scaffold, plan, or a required step, and cannot
        modify the code under test. Independence is checked against audit and
        commit authorship. The report is written somewhere implementers cannot
        alter.
    verifierIdentity:
        The verifier is a distinct authenticated principal identified by issuer
        and subject, not merely a new session. The excluded set is recorded
        before the run: scaffold author, descriptor and configuration author,
        onboarding author, plan author, every required implementer, the assessor
        of the same steps, delivery owner, merger, and integrator. The verifier
        records its signed context, session and attempt identity, and the pinned
        clean revision it observed.
        Verification grants cover running conformance and appending one report.
        The verifier may append its own report but may not alter an existing
        report, write implementation code, or write configuration. An external
        principal may verify if it is accepted by the project auth service. If
        no qualified independent principal exists, conformance stays blocked.
        The engineer cannot waive independence, including through a
        pre-authorization grant.
    reportAdmissibility:
        A report records checklist version, specification version,
        implementation version, descriptor version, claimed-capability
        inventory, environment fingerprint, verifier principal, pinned revision,
        per-scenario invocation, observed value, evidence hash, path-reached
        assertion, verdict, and trusted run time. The report hash is signed and
        anchored in the append-only audit chain. Reports are write-once.
        A pass expires on any specification, implementation, descriptor,
        capability, or environment change, or after 90 days from the trusted run
        time. A delta report reuses base evidence only for scenarios whose
        requirements, implementation, and environment are unchanged; it cites
        the base and covers every changed scenario once. Chained deltas cannot
        extend a base past its expiry. Evidence required by a live pass has a
        retention hold past the pass lifetime.
        A separate admission check records admissible or inadmissible with a
        reason. Missing evidence, non-independent verifier, unsigned or
        unanchored report, stale base, incomplete coverage, or a required
        scenario marked unsupported or not-applicable is inadmissible. A
        claimed specification gap remains a failure until an approved amendment
        and a re-run produce a new report. Adoption and conformance claims
        require an admissible report; an admissible report with a fail blocks
        the claim.
    verificationConformance:
        Cells cover: implementer verifier rejected while an independent
        principal passes a clean populated run; engineer-granted verifier
        capability for an excluded principal rejected; descriptor, configuration,
        or onboarding author rejected; external accepted principal allowed;
        implementation, descriptor, capability, or environment drift expiring a
        pass; day-90 expiry with retained evidence and GC; unsigned, unanchored,
        or post-write altered report rejected; expired or missing delta base
        rejected; duplicate or missing scenarios rejected; admissible failing
        report blocking adoption; and re-run after amendment approval producing
        a new report. Each cell records the pinned revision, environment,
        evidence hash, and admission reason.
    conformanceVerdicts:
        Verdicts are pass, fail, unsupported, or not-applicable. Capabilities
        are mapped to scenarios; only claimed capabilities require their
        scenarios, while core scenarios are always required. A matrix cell is
        reported separately and cannot be certified by a summary verdict. A
        pass expires when the spec version changes or after 90 days. Delta
        re-runs cite their base report and cover every required scenario exactly
        once. A failure is an implementation gap; a claimed specification gap
        becomes an amendment proposal requiring engineer approval and cannot be
        marked passed.
